WEBVTT

00:00:00.015 --> 00:00:03.536
Easy Science. Why Do Leaves Change Color?

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:06.336
In summer the leaves on the trees are green.

00:00:06.336 --> 00:00:11.448
In autumn many of them turn yellow, orange and red, and then they fall.

00:00:11.448 --> 00:00:12.163
Why?

00:00:12.163 --> 00:00:14.479
A leaf is like a small kitchen.

00:00:14.479 --> 00:00:18.983
It uses sunlight, air and water to make food for the tree.

00:00:18.983 --> 00:00:21.934
To do this, it needs a green material.

00:00:21.934 --> 00:00:25.188
This green material catches the light of the sun.

00:00:25.188 --> 00:00:29.140
There is so much of it in a leaf that the leaf looks green.

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:32.912
But leaves also have yellow and orange colors inside them.

00:00:32.912 --> 00:00:37.828
In summer we cannot see these colors, because the green covers them.

00:00:37.828 --> 00:00:40.717
In autumn the days get shorter and colder.

00:00:40.717 --> 00:00:42.364
There is less sunlight.

00:00:42.364 --> 00:00:45.816
The tree gets ready for winter and stops making food.

00:00:45.816 --> 00:00:49.530
The green material in the leaves breaks down and goes away.

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:54.746
Now the yellow and orange colors, which were always there, can be seen.

00:00:54.746 --> 00:01:00.711
Some trees also make a red color in their leaves during bright autumn days and cold nights.

00:01:00.711 --> 00:01:05.507
At last the tree closes the place where each leaf joins the branch.

00:01:05.507 --> 00:01:07.601
The leaf dies and falls.

00:01:07.601 --> 00:01:12.201
The tree rests through the winter and grows new green leaves in spring.
